To determine the cost of one egg when a dozen (12) eggs cost $3, you can simply divide the total cost by the number of eggs in a dozen:

\[
\text{Cost per egg} = \frac{\text{Total cost for 12 eggs}}{\text{Number of eggs in a dozen}}
= \frac{3}{12}
= \frac{1}{4}
= \$0.25
\]

So, one egg costs $0.25.
